WHY THIS IS SEPARATE FROM THE CODE
----------------------------------

The documents above are not API reference. They are argued prose in a particular
voice — the ADRs record what was considered and rejected, and why — and they are
the author's writing in the same sense the essays are. Licensing them under MIT
along with the code would grant anyone the right to modify that reasoning and
republish it under their own name with the attribution removed. That is not the
intent, and it would not have been noticed until it happened.

`NoDerivatives` is the load-bearing term here: it permits sharing the work
whole, with credit, and withholds the right to circulate an altered version of
it. `NonCommercial` is secondary and is present because there is no upside to
its absence.

